{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize a list to store the last four fib4 values: fib4(n-4), fib4(n-3), fib4(n-2), fib4(n-1)\n    dp = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = dp[0] + dp[1] + dp[2] + dp[3]\n        dp[0] = dp[1]\n        dp[1] = dp[2]\n        dp[2] = dp[3]\n        dp[3] = next_fib\n\n    return dp[3]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3.0\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd number of elements, return the middle element\n        return float(sorted_l[n // 2])\n    else:\n        # Even number of elements, return the average of the two middle elements\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (float(mid1) + float(mid2)) / 2.0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/48", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef is_palindrome(text: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if given string is a palindrome\n    >>> is_palindrome('')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('aba')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('aaaaa')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('zbcd')\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    # Normalize the string by converting to lowercase and removing non-alphanumeric characters.\n    normalized_text = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9]', '', text).lower()\n    # Compare the normalized string with its reverse.\n    return normalized_text == normalized_text[::-1]\n```"}
