{"task_id": "HumanEval/56", "solution": "```python\ndef correct_bracketing(brackets: str):\n    \"\"\" brackets is a string of \"<\" and \">\".\n    return True if every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket.\n    \"\"\"\n    balance = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '<':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == '>':\n            balance -= 1\n        # If balance ever drops below zero, it means a closing bracket appeared without a matching open one.\n        if balance < 0:\n            return False\n    # For a correctly bracketed string, the final balance must be zero.\n    return balance == 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n. Assume n > 1 and is not a prime.\"\"\"\n    largest_factor = 1\n\n    # Handle factor 2\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        largest_factor = 2\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Handle odd factors from 3 up to sqrt(n)\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        while n % i == 0:\n            largest_factor = i\n            n //= i\n        i += 2\n\n    # If n is still greater than 2, it means the remaining n is a prime factor and the largest.\n    if n > 2:\n        largest_factor = n\n\n    return largest_factor\n```"}
