{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts characters within each word of a string based on ASCII value, preserving word and space order.\n    A 'word' is any sequence of non-space characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Split the string into words and sequences of spaces, keeping the spaces as separate elements.\n    # The regex '(\\s+)' captures the delimiters (spaces).\n    parts = re.split(r'(\\s+)', s)\n\n    # Filter out any empty strings that might result from re.split, e.g., if s starts or ends with spaces.\n    filtered_parts = [part for part in parts if part]\n\n    processed_parts = []\n    for part in filtered_parts:\n        if part.strip():  # If the part contains non-whitespace characters (i.e., it's a word)\n            # Sort characters of the word based on their ASCII values in ascending order.\n            processed_parts.append(\"\".join(sorted(part)))\n        else:  # If the part is a sequence of spaces, keep it as is.\n            processed_parts.append(part)\n\n    # Join the processed parts back into a single string to form the final result.\n    return \"\".join(processed_parts)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/87", "solution": "```python\ndef get_row(lst, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds integer x in a nested list and returns a list of (row, column) coordinates.\n    Coordinates are sorted by rows in ascending order, then by columns in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    coordinates = []\n    for r_idx, row in enumerate(lst):\n        for c_idx, val in enumerate(row):\n            if val == x:\n                coordinates.append((r_idx, c_idx))\n\n    coordinates.sort(key=lambda coord: (coord[0], -coord[1]))\n    return coordinates\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of non-negative integers, return a copy of the given array after sorting,\n    you will sort the given array in ascending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is odd,\n    or sort it in descending order if the sum( first index value, last index value) is even.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) < 2:\n        return array.copy()\n\n    first_element = array[0]\n    last_element = array[-1]\n    sum_first_last = first_element + last_element\n\n    sorted_arr = array.copy()\n\n    if sum_first_last % 2 != 0:  # Odd sum, sort ascending\n        sorted_arr.sort()\n    else:  # Even sum, sort descending\n        sorted_arr.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    return sorted_arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "```python\ndef encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"Create a function encrypt that takes a string as an argument and\n    returns a string encrypted with the alphabet being rotated.\n    The alphabet should be rotated in a manner such that the letters\n    shift down by two multiplied to two places.\n    For example:\n    encrypt('hi') returns 'lm'\n    encrypt('asdfghjkl') returns 'ewhjklnop'\n    encrypt('gf') returns 'kj'\n    encrypt('et') returns 'ix'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    def _shift_char(char: str, shift: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Shifts a lowercase English character by a given amount, wrapping around the alphabet. Non-lowercase characters are returned unchanged.\"\"\"\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            start_ascii = ord('a')\n            shifted_ascii = start_ascii + (ord(char) - start_ascii + shift) % 26\n            return chr(shifted_ascii)\n        return char\n\n    encrypted_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        encrypted_chars.append(_shift_char(char, 4)) # Shift value is 2 multiplied by 2, which is 4.\n    return \"\".join(encrypted_chars)\n```"}
